course: dictionary
lesson: 16107
title: Wellbeing
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Wellbeing is a noun. It means being healthy, happy and comfortable in both body and mind. You can say someone has good wellbeing, or that a school cares about the wellbeing of its children.
explain: You can look at the word's parts to help you. Well means good or healthy, and being means the state you are in. Put them together and wellbeing means the state of feeling good. «Our school has a wellbeing week in the autumn.» Here wellbeing week is a week for looking after how children feel and stay healthy.
explain: Wellbeing covers many things: sleep, food, exercise, friendships, feelings and asking for help. «Good sleep, healthy food and time with friends all help your wellbeing.» Each one helps your body or mind feel well.
explain: Some phrases tell you which part of wellbeing is meant. Physical wellbeing is about your body. Mental wellbeing is about your mind and feelings. «Asking for help when you feel worried is part of looking after your mental wellbeing.»
fact: Wellbeing means being healthy, happy and comfortable in body and mind.
fact: Wellbeing can also be written as well-being, with a hyphen.
fact: Wellbeing is uncountable, so say «good wellbeing», not «a wellbeing».
fact: Physical wellbeing is about your body, and mental wellbeing is about your mind and feelings.
fact: Sleep, healthy food, exercise, friendships and asking for help all support wellbeing.
exercise: «Good sleep and healthy food help your wellbeing.» What does wellbeing mean here? | Being late for school | Being in a great hurry | *Being healthy, happy and comfortable in body and mind | Being very rich with lots of money
exercise: The word wellbeing is made of two parts. Which part means good or healthy? | Wellbeing | *Well | Being | Bee
exercise: Which is a good way to look after your wellbeing? | Staying up all night | Never going outside | *Talking to a friend when you feel worried | Skipping every meal
test: «Our class had a wellbeing lesson about sleep and friendship.» What is a wellbeing lesson about? | *Looking after health, feelings and friendships | Old castles and kings | Football scores | Long division
test: Which phrase means looking after your mind and feelings? | Good posture | Physical wellbeing | *Mental wellbeing | Wellbeing week
exam: Pick the best meaning of wellbeing. | Being very tired after a long run | Being away from home | *Being healthy, happy and comfortable in body and mind | Being top of the class
